From 7393cb665b278cf85b3c81013f7e2660f495b65b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 07/26] media: i2c: add a driver for the GalaxyCore GC02M2

The GC02M2 is a 2 megapixel 1/5" raw Bayer sensor with a single-lane
MIPI CSI-2 interface, used as the front camera of the PINE64 PineTab 2.

Ported from the Rockchip vendor driver to the mainline V4L2 subdev and CCI
APIs, following gc05a2. One mode, 1600x1200 SRGGB10 at 30 fps, 336 MHz link
frequency. The vendor's total gain (1/64 steps, 0x40 unity) is exposed as the
analogue gain and split into the sensor's analogue step table plus a digital
remainder exactly as the vendor driver did. Exposure and frame length are
14-bit registers; the chip is identified once at probe.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
